{"duration_api_ms":58055,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"f3ddfed4-9e11-4dbd-ae52-d249a4bbef44","total_cost_usd":0.2008372,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":30679,"cache_read_input_tokens":35551,"output_tokens":5432,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1850},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":30679,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1816,"cache_read_input_tokens":31229,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3772,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3772},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":16608,"outputTokens":15,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.016683,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":5432,"cacheReadInputTokens":35551,"cacheCreationInputTokens":30679,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.1841542,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":1850,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"req-1\",\"requirement\":\"At least 512MB compressed in-memory (zram) swap configured on node1\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"zram module loaded with num_devices=1, zram0 sized to 1G (>512MB) with lzo compression, mkswap+swapon succeeded; /proc/swaps and zramctl confirm a 1G lzo-compressed zram0 swap device is active.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-c335997af28c420c\",\"cmd-bda6bca352ff4f5c\",\"cmd-dc37bdd294d94eb4\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2\",\"requirement\":\"zram swap preferred over disk-backed swap\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"zram0 configured with priority 100 vs /dev/vda2 at priority -2. Under induced real memory pressure (tmpfs fill via dd), /proc/swaps and zramctl showed 528M/540928KB of swap usage landing entirely on zram0 while the disk partition remained at 0 used, directly demonstrating preference in practice, not just configuration.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-dc37bdd294d94eb4\",\"cmd-7895881cbd2a4699\",\"cmd-eed2b1c4fda34b70\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3\",\"requirement\":\"zram swap active at boot (persists across reboot)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"zram-swap.service was enabled pre-reboot; a healthy pre-reboot baseline (boot_id 2fc81aed..., active zram0 swap) was captured, a real reboot was issued and acknowledged, the connection dropped and polling confirmed unreachability during the disruption window, and post-reboot state shows a new boot_id (71a394c9...), zram-swap.service active/enabled, and a fresh 1G zram0 swap device at priority 100 with no manual intervention — a complete bounded disruption-and-recovery cycle.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-0d29775bbd37433c\",\"cmd-e0f6a03c68c84a59\",\"cmd-4dd495f831fb48ee\",\"cmd-fd2eff3328a24b0f\",\"cmd-d5c7594c57cd4f35\",\"cmd-4f8d353e6c284492\",\"cmd-5558c09e670e49b3\"]}],\"confidence\":0.94,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.9,\"summary\":\"The executor iterated through several troubleshooting steps (an initial zram-init.sh version missing num_devices handling failed once via cmd-6174b6d1ff324ce1, and a premature swapoff/zramctl-reset attempt in cmd-9b5d96b9140744c0 failed harmlessly) before arriving at the working configuration; these left no residue since the final /etc/modprobe.d/zram.conf, /usr/local/sbin/zram-init.sh, and zram-swap.service all reflect the corrected, working versions confirmed by the after_executor snapshot showing zero failed services. The tmpfs (/dev/shm) was temporarily remounted from 1000M to 3000M and filled with two 900M files to induce real memory pressure for the preference test (cmd-7895881cbd2a4699, cmd-eed2b1c4fda34b70); this was a bounded, low-risk, purposeful mutation directly supporting req-2 and was fully reverted afterward (files removed, tmpfs size restored) in cmd-ab48955321324c02. No unnecessary mutations remained in the final state; temp-file and listening-socket deltas between after_prepare and after_executor are attributable solely to the reboot (new boot-scoped systemd-private dirs, reboot.log, and PIDs), not to executor residue.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets\",\"cmd-ab48955321324c02\",\"cmd-9b5d96b9140744c0\",\"cmd-6174b6d1ff324ce1\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All material outcomes are satisfied with direct evidence: a 1G lzo-compressed zram swap device was configured, verified as preferred over disk swap under an actual memory-pressure test (swap usage landed entirely on zram0), and shown to survive a real reboot with the service enabled and the device automatically recreated with no manual steps. The mandatory restart evidence protocol was also completed cleanly, corroborated independently by the fixed after_executor boot-identity snapshot. Troubleshooting iterations during setup were transient and left no residue; the one deliberate tmpfs-size mutation used for the preference test was bounded and fully reverted.\",\"limitations\":[\"Package-health snapshots were unavailable (timed out) both before and after, so native package-manager consistency could not be independently cross-checked, though this is unrelated to the zram task.\",\"The memory-pressure verification relied on manual tmpfs fills rather than a dedicated stress tool (stress-ng/stress were unavailable), which is a reasonable substitute but a slightly less standard method of inducing swap pressure.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"At least 512MB compressed in-memory (zram) swap configured on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"zram module loaded with num_devices=1, zram0 sized to 1G (>512MB) with lzo compression, mkswap+swapon succeeded; /proc/swaps and zramctl confirm a 1G lzo-compressed zram0 swap device is active.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c335997af28c420c","cmd-bda6bca352ff4f5c","cmd-dc37bdd294d94eb4"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"zram swap preferred over disk-backed swap","status":"satisfied","summary":"zram0 configured with priority 100 vs /dev/vda2 at priority -2. Under induced real memory pressure (tmpfs fill via dd), /proc/swaps and zramctl showed 528M/540928KB of swap usage landing entirely on zram0 while the disk partition remained at 0 used, directly demonstrating preference in practice, not just configuration.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dc37bdd294d94eb4","cmd-7895881cbd2a4699","cmd-eed2b1c4fda34b70"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"zram swap active at boot (persists across reboot)","status":"satisfied","summary":"zram-swap.service was enabled pre-reboot; a healthy pre-reboot baseline (boot_id 2fc81aed..., active zram0 swap) was captured, a real reboot was issued and acknowledged, the connection dropped and polling confirmed unreachability during the disruption window, and post-reboot state shows a new boot_id (71a394c9...), zram-swap.service active/enabled, and a fresh 1G zram0 swap device at priority 100 with no manual intervention — a complete bounded disruption-and-recovery cycle.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0d29775bbd37433c","cmd-e0f6a03c68c84a59","cmd-4dd495f831fb48ee","cmd-fd2eff3328a24b0f","cmd-d5c7594c57cd4f35","cmd-4f8d353e6c284492","cmd-5558c09e670e49b3"]}],"confidence":0.94,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"The executor iterated through several troubleshooting steps (an initial zram-init.sh version missing num_devices handling failed once via cmd-6174b6d1ff324ce1, and a premature swapoff/zramctl-reset attempt in cmd-9b5d96b9140744c0 failed harmlessly) before arriving at the working configuration; these left no residue since the final /etc/modprobe.d/zram.conf, /usr/local/sbin/zram-init.sh, and zram-swap.service all reflect the corrected, working versions confirmed by the after_executor snapshot showing zero failed services. The tmpfs (/dev/shm) was temporarily remounted from 1000M to 3000M and filled with two 900M files to induce real memory pressure for the preference test (cmd-7895881cbd2a4699, cmd-eed2b1c4fda34b70); this was a bounded, low-risk, purposeful mutation directly supporting req-2 and was fully reverted afterward (files removed, tmpfs size restored) in cmd-ab48955321324c02. No unnecessary mutations remained in the final state; temp-file and listening-socket deltas between after_prepare and after_executor are attributable solely to the reboot (new boot-scoped systemd-private dirs, reboot.log, and PIDs), not to executor residue.","evidence_ids":["global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","cmd-ab48955321324c02","cmd-9b5d96b9140744c0","cmd-6174b6d1ff324ce1"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied with direct evidence: a 1G lzo-compressed zram swap device was configured, verified as preferred over disk swap under an actual memory-pressure test (swap usage landed entirely on zram0), and shown to survive a real reboot with the service enabled and the device automatically recreated with no manual steps. The mandatory restart evidence protocol was also completed cleanly, corroborated independently by the fixed after_executor boot-identity snapshot. Troubleshooting iterations during setup were transient and left no residue; the one deliberate tmpfs-size mutation used for the preference test was bounded and fully reverted.","limitations":["Package-health snapshots were unavailable (timed out) both before and after, so native package-manager consistency could not be independently cross-checked, though this is unrelated to the zram task.","The memory-pressure verification relied on manual tmpfs fills rather than a dedicated stress tool (stress-ng/stress were unavailable), which is a reasonable substitute but a slightly less standard method of inducing swap pressure."]},"ttft_ms":26915,"type":"result","duration_ms":56737,"uuid":"67ab0530-4f25-4420-b4a8-edffae005f0a","ttft_stream_ms":760,"time_to_request_ms":42,"first_content_frame_ms":1107,"queued_turn_count":0}
